            <div xml:id="d363">

                <pb facs="0444" n="432" sameAs="frus:frus1942v01/pg432"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">701.0090/362: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Harrison</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Bern</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1942-06-13"
                            >June 13, 1942</date>.<lb/>[Received June 13—5:02 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2705. Exchange negotiations—Far East. Department’s 1521, 12th. Swiss Legation,
                    Tokyo telephoned Swiss Foreign Office June 13 following: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Japanese Government states there is discrepancy in number of names on
                            Admiral Nomura’s list and Japanese list of Japanese to be embarked on
                                <hi rendition="#italic">Gripsholm</hi>. Discrepancy is approximately
                            160 including <pb facs="0445" n="433" xml:id="pg433"/> not only
                            non-official but also some officials. Japanese Government states that
                                <hi rendition="#italic">Asama Maru</hi> will depart on June 15 but
                            that corresponding number of American officials and non-officials will
                            be left behind if above discrepancies are not settled by then.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Harrison</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
